---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Aaron’s Dev Experiments">
	<section class="topic-header">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>

		<h1>About This Site</h1>

		<p class="intro">
			A personal technical notebook for the projects, experiments, and
			engineering problems I spend my free time working through.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="about-content">
		<h2>About Me</h2>

		<div class="about-intro">
			<img class="about-photo" src="/images/me.jpg" alt="Aaron" />

			<div>
				<p>
					I'm Aaron, a construction worker turned retailer turned
					computer science graduate, now trying to turn all of that
					into a career in software development.
				</p>

				<p>
					Programming has been a hobby of mine for many years. I’ve
					always enjoyed working with my hands, building things, and
					figuring out how they fit together. Software has been a
					natural extension of that.
				</p>

				<p>
					These days, that mostly means software engineering,
					graphics, terrain systems, tools, and whatever technical
					problem happens to catch my attention.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>What I'm Working On</h2>

		<p>
			Most of the material here currently comes from Plane Voxel Lab, an
			experimental C++ / OpenGL project where I have been exploring
			terrain representation, rendering, spatial systems, and editable
			world geometry.
		</p>

		<p>
			The site is intentionally broader than that particular project. I
			plan on continuing these experiments—following some to more
			interesting conclusions, while ending others as a single article.
			The long-term goal is to build and publish a game along the way, and
			I wanted room here for all of that.
		</p>

		<h2>Why Document It?</h2>

		<p>
			It is as much for me as it is for any potential audience. The
			process of writing about an implementation forces me to sit down and
			pore through the details—what worked, what didn't, why it worked,
			etc. It gives me a way to organize my thoughts outside of the code
			itself. If anyone else finds any of it useful along the way, that's
			awesome too.
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
